ft-hb: load HarfBuzz without RTLD_GLOBAL

The autofitter dlopens libharfbuzz.so.0 the first time it shapes a
font, and RTLD_GLOBAL puts HarfBuzz and everything under it - this
library, libpng16, zlib, bz2 - into the process-wide symbol scope from
that moment on. Any module dlopened afterwards then binds those names
to the global copies before its own.

Steam's arm64 client (1792099137, 2026-10-14) ships a static libpng
1.6.37 inside steamui.so, friendsui.so and vgui2_s.so, with every
png_* symbol exported. steamui.so is loaded before the autofitter
runs and binds to its own copy; friendsui.so is loaded after login and
binds png_create_info_struct to /usr/lib/libpng16.so.16. The png_ptr
steamui made with Valve's build crosses into the image's build, whose
struct layout differs, and the client segfaults a second after the
login screen - back to the launcher. Verified with LD_DEBUG=scopes: the
global scope gains libharfbuzz, libfreetype, libpng16 right before
friendsui.so is loaded.

FreeType itself takes every HarfBuzz symbol through dlsym on the
handle, so RTLD_GLOBAL buys it nothing. RTLD_DEFAULT is still tried
first, so a process that linked HarfBuzz keeps sharing that one.

--- a/src/autofit/ft-hb.c
+++ b/src/autofit/ft-hb.c
@@ -101,25 +101,25 @@
 #else /* !_WIN32 */

 #  ifdef RTLD_DEFAULT
-#    define FT_RTLD_FLAGS RTLD_LAZY | RTLD_GLOBAL
     lib             = RTLD_DEFAULT;
     version_atleast = DLSYM( lib, hb_version_atleast );
-#  else
-#    define FT_RTLD_FLAGS RTLD_LAZY
 #  endif

     if ( !version_atleast )
     {
       /* Load the HarfBuzz library.
        *
-       * We never close the library, since we opened it with RTLD_GLOBAL.
-       * This is important for the case where we are using HarfBuzz as a
-       * shared library, and we want to use the symbols from the library in
-       * other shared libraries or clients.  HarfBuzz holds onto global
+       * Without RTLD_GLOBAL: every symbol FreeType needs comes through
+       * DLSYM on this handle, and a global HarfBuzz drags its dependency
+       * tree (this library, libpng, zlib) into the process-wide search
+       * scope, where it interposes copies a client carries in its own
+       * modules.
+       *
+       * We never close the library.  HarfBuzz holds onto global
        * variables, and closing the library will cause them to be
        * invalidated.
        */
-      lib = dlopen( FT_LIBHARFBUZZ, FT_RTLD_FLAGS );
+      lib = dlopen( FT_LIBHARFBUZZ, RTLD_LAZY );
       if ( !lib )
         goto Fail;
       version_atleast = DLSYM( lib, hb_version_atleast );
